---
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import { mailto, site } from "../../data/site";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "13 October 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Toward Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Toward (Interview Tracker) by Visify Apps."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/toward"
>
  <Section narrow>
    <p class="label">Legal · Toward</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">
      Updated {lastUpdated} · Package <code>com.visify.toward</code>
    </p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>Toward</strong> (Interview
        Tracker), published by {site.shortName}, handles information. Toward is
        designed to be <strong>local-first</strong>: your applications and
        rounds stay on your device unless you choose optional cloud backup.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information we process</h2>
      <h3>1.1 On your device (local)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Company names, roles, statuses, notes, job links, and interview /
          assessment rounds you enter
        </li>
        <li>
          Resume version labels and optional resume files you upload (stored in
          the app’s private documents folder)
        </li>
        <li>App preferences (theme, no-reply auto-mark, quieter-ads window)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This data is stored in a local database on your phone. {site.shortName}
        cannot read it unless you use optional cloud backup.
      </p>

      <h3>1.2 Optional account &amp; cloud backup</h3>
      <p>If you sign in for cloud backup, we process:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Email address and authentication credentials (via Firebase
          Authentication — email/password or Google Sign-In)
        </li>
        <li>
          Companies, rounds, and resume <strong>metadata</strong> (name, note,
          filenames) in Cloud Firestore under your user id
        </li>
        <li>Backup timestamps and counts</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Resume PDF/DOC file bytes are not uploaded.</strong> On restore,
        Toward only re-links files that still exist on that same device. Backup
        is optional — you can use Toward without an account.
      </p>

      <h3>1.3 Advertising (Android)</h3>
      <p>
        The App shows ads through <strong>Google AdMob</strong>. Google and its
        partners may collect device and advertising identifiers, IP address,
        approximate location derived from IP, interaction data, and diagnostic
        information to serve and measure ads, including personalized ads where
        allowed. You may see options related to ad personalization based on your
        region and device settings.
      </p>
      <p>
        See Google’s
        <a
          href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">Privacy Policy</a
        >
        and
        <a
          href="https://support.google.com/admob/answer/6128543"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">AdMob &amp; privacy</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h3>1.4 Diagnostics</h3>
      <p>
        When Firebase is configured for a build, Toward may use Firebase
        Analytics and Crashlytics for stability and aggregate usage. We do not
        sell your personal information.
      </p>

      <h3>1.5 Notifications</h3>
      <p>
        Toward may schedule a <strong>local</strong> nudge after a round’s
        scheduled time so you can log pass or fail. It does not use Firebase
        Cloud Messaging or exact-alarm / calendar permissions for these nudges.
      </p>

      <h2>2. How we use information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To provide interview tracking on your device</li>
        <li>To provide optional backup/restore if you sign in</li>
        <li>To show ads and keep the App free</li>
        <li>To improve reliability and security</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Sharing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google Firebase</strong> — optional auth and backup</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google AdMob / advertising partners</strong> — ads and
          measurement
        </li>
        <li>We do not sell personal data to data brokers</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Retention</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Local data remains until you clear it in Settings or uninstall the App
        </li>
        <li>
          Cloud backup remains until you delete the backup/account or request
          deletion
        </li>
        <li>Ad-related data is retained per Google’s policies</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the App without signing in</li>
        <li>Clear all local data from Settings</li>
        <li>
          Delete cloud backup / account from Settings → Cloud backup (see
          <a href="/privacy/toward-deletion">account deletion</a>)
        </li>
        <li>
          Adjust device ad / notification settings, or use the in-app rewarded
          option to pause ads temporarily when offered
        </li>
        <li>
          Email us for help:
          <a href={mailto("Toward privacy / deletion")}>{site.email}</a>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Children</h2>
      <p>
        Toward is aimed at students and job seekers. It is not directed at
        children under 13 (or the minimum age required in your country). We do
        not knowingly collect personal information from children.
      </p>

      <h2>7. International processing</h2>
      <p>
        If you use Firebase or AdMob, data may be processed on servers outside
        your country, including by Google, subject to their safeguards and
        applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy. The “Updated” date at the top will change when
        we do. Continued use of the App after an update means you accept the
        revised policy.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        {site.shortName}<br />
        Email: <a href={mailto("Toward privacy")}>{site.email}</a><br />
        App: Toward — Interview Tracker (<code>com.visify.toward</code>)
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href="/privacy">← Company privacy</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .meta {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
</style>
